{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>יבש</b> — And he cannot speak; therefore one of the Geonim said: כחי הפך חכי. In my opinion: because the vapor of generation, which binds everything and sustains the body, is called כח, therefore it says יבש, as happens to an old man advanced in days." "<b>ומלקוחי</b> — from the root of ומלקחיה, and if it is not on its pattern." "<b>ולעפר מות</b> — to the dust of the sons of death, like גבורתך במלחמה." "<b>ותשפתני</b> — like שפות הסיר."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:13.659248059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}